---
const cmsLimits = [
  "Only the fields the CMS was set up to show",
  "A new page means a ticket, then a sprint",
  "Ideas wait on a developer's calendar",
  "The campaign ships after the moment has passed",
];

const prompts = [
  {
    who: "marketing",
    ask: "Build a landing page for group bookings with our usual hero and FAQ.",
    result: "+ src/pages/group-bookings.astro",
  },
  {
    who: "founder",
    ask: "Add a comparison page against Calendly with a feature table.",
    result: "+ src/pages/vs-calendly.astro",
  },
  {
    who: "support",
    ask: "Turn this week's top customer questions into help articles.",
    result: "+ 4 files in content/helpDocs/en/",
  },
  {
    who: "writer",
    ask: "Link every post that mentions previews to the new guide.",
    result: "~ 7 files in content/blog/en/",
  },
];
---

<section class="page grid gap-12 py-section md:grid-cols-12 md:gap-10" id="agent" data-reveal>
  <div class="md:col-span-5">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-light tracking-display text-ink md:text-4xl">Ask for whole new pages, not just edits.</h2>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-measure text-muted">
      A CMS lets people fill in the fields someone built for them. With an agent on the repo, your team can ask for
      things that used to take a sprint, and each one lands as a draft to review before it ships.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid gap-10 md:col-span-7 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-8">
    <div>
      <p class="label">with a cms</p>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 border-t border-line pt-6">
        {cmsLimits.map((item) => (
          <li class="text-muted">{item}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="label">with orso and an agent</p>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-6 border-t border-line pt-6">
        {prompts.map((prompt) => (
          <li>
            <p class="text-sm">
              <span class="font-medium text-accent">{prompt.who}</span>
              <span class="text-ink"> “{prompt.ask}”</span>
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-muted">draft ready · {prompt.result}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
